Public Suffix List, https://publicsuffix.org (MPL-2.0, https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/). src/tls/x509/psl.mojo is generated
from it by tools/gen_psl.py (the version and commit are in the file header) and keeps the MPL-2.0 terms: the data is
unmodified apart from the filtering the generator documents. Its source is the list at publicsuffix.org.

2. Test vectors and test data (tests/, tools/)

Project Wycheproof, https://github.com/C2SP/wycheproof (Apache-2.0): tests/vec/wyche-aead.txt and wyche-mac.txt are
converted from its testvectors_v1 files; the asymmetric vectors (x25519, x448, ECDH, ECDSA, RSA) are fetched by
tests/gate_asym.sh from a clone at test time and are not distributed here.

x509-limbo, https://github.com/C2SP/x509-limbo (Apache-2.0): fetched at test time by tools/limbo_fetch.sh (not in this
repository); tests/limbo_known.txt lists case ids only.

RFC 8448 (TLS 1.3 example traces), RFC 7748, RFC 5903, RFC 6979 and RFC 8439: known-answer values quoted in
tests/vectors/rfc8448.txt, tests/vectors/kat.txt and tests/kat.mojo. RFC text is Copyright (c) IETF Trust and the persons
identified as the document authors; code components and test values are used under the Revised BSD licence of the IETF
Trust's Legal Provisions.

Captured ClientHello messages in tests/vectors/ch_*.hex come from curl, OpenSSL, Python and Chromium (Vivaldi) talking to a local
test socket; they contain no secrets.

3. Tools run against mojo-tls, never shipped

tlsfuzzer (GPL-2.0, https://github.com/tlsfuzzer/tlsfuzzer) and testssl.sh (GPL-2.0) are cloned into .work/tools by the
local matrix (tests/matrix.sh) and run as separate programs; their code is not part of this repository. OpenSSL,
curl, Python `cryptography`, Firefox and Chromium serve as oracles and interop peers in the same way.
